-- title:
--   Theorem 14 — if F_r is a KŁ function, bounded proximal ADMM iterates have finite length and converge to a KKT point
-- statement:
--   Suppose Assumption 1 holds and $\{(x^k,z^k,y^k)\}_{k\ge0}$, generated by Algorithm 1 or Algorithm 2, is bounded. If the regularized augmented Lagrangian
--   $$F_r(x,z,y,x',y')=L_r(x,z,y)+T_1\|A^*(y-y')\|^2+\tfrac{C_1}2\|x-x'\|^2$$
--   is a Kurdyka–Łojasiewicz function, then:
--   1. the sequence has finite length:
--   $$\sum_{k\ge0}\|x^{k+1}-x^k\|<+\infty,\qquad\sum_{k\ge0}\|z^{k+1}-z^k\|<+\infty,\qquad\sum_{k\ge0}\|y^{k+1}-y^k\|<+\infty;$$
--   2. the sequence converges to a KKT point $(\hat x,\hat z,\hat y)$ of problem (1): $-A^*\hat y=\nabla h(\hat x)$, $\hat y\in\partial g(\hat z)$, $\hat z=A\hat x$.
--
--   This is the main global convergence result of the paper for both the proximal and the proximal-linearized nonconvex ADMM with variable metrics.
--
--   **Formalization Note** "KŁ function" is the published `IsKLFunction` on the 5-fold Euclidean (`WithLp 2`) product, for the specific $F_r$ with the constants $T_1$, $C_1$ of §2.2 (so the hypothesis depends on the algorithm and the parameters); the KL inequality is read as $\varphi'(\cdot)\|v\|\ge1$ for every $v\in\partial F_r(u)$ (i.e. $\operatorname{dist}(0,\emptyset)=+\infty$), and $\eta$ is a positive real, equivalent to the paper's $\eta\in(0,+\infty]$. Finite length is summability of the norms of the increments.
-- source:
--   Boţ and Nguyen, The proximal ADMM in the nonconvex setting, arXiv:1801.01994v2, p. 21, Theorem 14, (65)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_NonconvexSplitting_Shared_StandingAssumptions
import Definitions.Def_NonconvexSplitting_Shared_LimitingSubdiff
import Definitions.Def_NonconvexSplitting_ADMMKL_KLProperty
import Definitions.Def_BotNguyenADMM_KL_Setting
open NonconvexSplitting.Shared NonconvexSplitting.ADMMKL BotNguyenADMM.KL
open Filter Topology
open scoped RealInnerProductSpace

namespace BotNguyenADMM.KL

/-- Theorem 14 (p. 21). Suppose Assumption 1 holds and `{(xᵏ, zᵏ, yᵏ)}` is a bounded sequence
generated by Algorithm 1 or Algorithm 2. If the regularized augmented Lagrangian `F_r` (p. 14,
with the constants `T₁`, `C₁` of p. 10) is a KŁ function on `ℝⁿ × ℝᵐ × ℝᵐ × ℝⁿ × ℝᵐ`, then
(i) the sequence has finite length (65): `∑‖xᵏ⁺¹ − xᵏ‖ < ∞`, `∑‖zᵏ⁺¹ − zᵏ‖ < ∞`,
`∑‖yᵏ⁺¹ − yᵏ‖ < ∞`; and
(ii) it converges to a KKT point `(x̂, ẑ, ŷ)` of problem (1): `−A*ŷ = ∇h(x̂)`, `ŷ ∈ ∂g(ẑ)`,
`ẑ = Ax̂`. -/
theorem theorem_14 {n m : ℕ} (v : Variant) (P : Data n m) (hA : Assumption1 v P)
    (x : ℕ → E n) (z y : ℕ → E m) (hrun : IsRun v P x z y)
    (hbdd : Bornology.IsBounded (Set.range fun k => pack3 (x k) (z k) (y k)))
    (hKL : IsKLFunction (Fr v P)) :
    (Summable (fun k => ‖x (k + 1) - x k‖) ∧ Summable (fun k => ‖z (k + 1) - z k‖) ∧
      Summable (fun k => ‖y (k + 1) - y k‖)) ∧
    ∃ (xh : E n) (zh yh : E m), IsKKTPoint P xh zh yh ∧
      Tendsto x atTop (𝓝 xh) ∧ Tendsto z atTop (𝓝 zh) ∧ Tendsto y atTop (𝓝 yh) := by sorry

end BotNguyenADMM.KL
